  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trade Mission Palestinian ICT sector</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ICT sector in the Palestinian Territories employed around 9000 individuals in some 700 different companies in the West Bank and Gaza combined. In 2022, the ICT sector accounted for about 4% ($651 million) of Palestinian Gross Domestic Product (GDP), and was growing slowly until October 2023.Since 2023 the Palestinian economy was hit by multiple significant shocks. The World Bank estimates that about half a million jobs have been lost, which also extends to the ICT sector. Fighting in Gaza resulted in an enormous toll on Gaza&#x2019;s tech sector, where many talented individuals were killed, lost their jobs and clients or fled. But it also affected companies in the West Bank as relationships with many Israeli clients were severed and the Palestinian government and public sector also struggled with a significant drop in income. The need to export IT services has only increased due to these developments. Recovery of the Palestinian ICT sector lies in the effective engagement with international markets. Despite many challenges, the Palestinian ICT sector with a highly-skilled work-force, not restricted by time or location, has capacity to serve many clients. Offering Palestinian IT outsourcing services to the Netherlands and the European Union (EU) region is a very viable option therefor, which can make a significant contribution to the local economy and jobs needed as well as offer the Netherlands/EU access to quality IT offshoring solutions. Hence the organisation of this IT trade mission to establish connections and introduce Palestinian IT outsourcing services and solutions to the Dutch/EU private sector.</narrative>
  </description>
